WEBVTT

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.000
So you're Sparda's son?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.420
So what if I am, Milkman?

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.960
The answer is obvious.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.420
I'll take your soul.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.690
Hey, if you're going to help me out,
could you do it a little more quietly?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.400
Help you? Don't get the wrong idea, pal.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.860
I just targeted a demon, that's all.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.610
A white demon.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.930
You did! You definitely promised me!

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.140
Like hell I did.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.810
Yes you did! You said
you'd take me to the ocean.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.680
What the hell would you
want to do at the ocean?

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:02.610
Play, obviously! Go swimming, get
sunburned, eat good food, that stuff.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.690
You can do that stuff anywhere.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:07.030
Doing it at the ocean is
what gives it meaning!

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.280
Okay, fine.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.160
Really?!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.990
I'll lend you the car, so go by yourself.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:18.040
Yeah, right! If I could drive
myself, there's no way I'd ask you...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.580
What?! I dare you to say that again!

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.250
Please don't misunderstand me. I just...

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.090
Shut up! Get out of here!

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.510
Thanks for waiting!

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.760
What's going on with them?

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.970
Oh, that guy said the boss's
strawberry sundaes weren't good.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.220
Strawberry sundaes...

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.430
You mean these?

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.730
If I offended you, I apologize.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.320
I only meant to say that using
slightly less sugar would make them--

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.650
You bastard! You're still saying that?!

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.570
I don't even want your
money now! Hurry up and--

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.570
Hold on, Fredi.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.490
I've got something of an
attachment to the sundaes here myself.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.410
But they seem to be sweeter than usual today.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.540
That man is right.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.630
He got all sulky...

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.430
Apparently he's a sensitive guy
behind that gruff face of his.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.890
It seems I've hurt his feelings.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.060
Devil!

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.190
Please, someone help me! Sh-She's a devil!

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:31.990
Yep, I'm a devil. And what about you?

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.000
That's right...

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.540
I'm a devil, too!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.470
Are you still alive?

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.810
I've got a question for you.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:06.980
Do you know about the white devil
that's been showing up around here lately?

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:10.820
Nope. Even if I did, I
wouldn't tell you who...

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.610
That's a lie! I was lying!

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:18.450
I totally know who he is.
The guy they call Sparda's apprentice.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.240
Apprentice?

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.080
Yes, that's right.
He's apparently extremely tough,

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.920
and the rumor is that when
he takes a sword in his hand,

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.250
one or two thousand demons
get killed in a split second!

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.680
Um, are we through yet, Miss? Can I...

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.950
...eat you now?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.790
Anyway, I heard rumors like that around town.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:07.880
I see. So you called me here to
pass the word on to me, is that it?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.670
That's right.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.460
How unusually kind of you.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.380
I just thought I'd give you a little warning.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:18.550
It'd be a pity if I ended up
killing him instead of you, right?

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.680
Since it kinda seems like
there's history between you two.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:22.600
Maybe so.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.310
Sorry, but he asked for me by name.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:28.900
I won't let anyone interfere.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.010
A demon who fought to
protect the human world...

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:04.640
My mentor... Sparda, the dark knight.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.980
It's been 2,000 years since that battle.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:15.440
And now the one who has
appeared before us is not you,

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.240
but your son Dante.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.140
Did I startle you?

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:45.640
Yeah.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.640
Liar.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.430
Why do you say that?

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.440
Because you're not startled at all!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:56.280
Sheesh, I can't tell if you're kind
or cold. You're the opposite of Dante.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.360
Opposite?

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:01.450
Yep. Because I can't tell
if Dante is cold or kind.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.450
So in the end, you can't tell, huh?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.660
Oh, I do know one thing!

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.040
You both love strawberry sundaes
even though you're grown-ups.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:17.960
What are you doing?

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.930
People-watching, perhaps.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:27.510
You sure seem to have time on your hands.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.600
It's pretty peaceful, huh?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.730
Yes...

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:41.110
It really is peaceful.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.950
I'd like to have times like these forever.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:01.050
Ah, Lord Modeus always seems so placid.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.390
I can hardly believe that
the two of you are twins.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:14.140
But really, what a waste. I wonder why
Lord Modeus abandoned swordsmanship?

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:17.520
I'm told that long ago, his skill
with his sword was great enough

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.480
to make the whole demon world tremble.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:26.240
Well, I suppose he felt he could never hope
to beat you, Lord Baul, and so he gave up.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:37.880
Sparda entrusted his true
strength and will to Modeus, not to me.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.880
L-L-Lord Baul, I can't breathe...

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.600
Ouch...

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:47.430
What would the likes of you
know about my brother and I?

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:54.310
Oh, I know what you have in mind.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:10:00.270
You intend to go there, don't you?
To the Devil May Cry.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.960
Throw it back this way!

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.460
Hey, wait!

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:28.970
And get this! Dante eats
nothing but pizza every day!

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.600
What do you think of an
adult who acts like that?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.520
Well, it's not for me.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.640
If I were going to date someone,
no way would it be a guy like that!

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.560
He's lucky if he gets one job a week.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.360
Oh, Dante runs an odd-job
business called the "Devil May Cry."

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.150
But no matter how many jobs Morrison brings,

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.320
he just screws them all up,
and it's a real problem!

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.450
And it seems like he owes Lady a lot of
money, too. Honestly, Dante is just so...

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.960
Oh no! I'm on dinner duty today!

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.040
If I don't get back quick, the head
of the orphanage will yell at me.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.880
Well, I'm off!

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:05.550
Hey!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.720
Will you be at loose ends tomorrow too?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:11.220
You will, right? I'll make
you a strawberry sundae, then!

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.180
Come to the Devil May Cry tomorrow!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.850
That's a promise!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:26.190
Huh, a strawberry sundae, eh?

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.070
What a cute little girl.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:29.820
Yes.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:34.290
No doubt that girl would grieve too...

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:38.330
...if Dante were to end up dead.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.330
"Closed until further notice"?

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:27.300
Heh, did he go off to train
in the mountains or something?

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.610
Dante isn't here.

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.150
I see.

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:53.910
Why? Your opponent is Sparda, isn't he?

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:57.030
So why would you fight Dante?

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.370
Sparda is dead.

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.160
He's alive! I'm sure that
somewhere out there he's...

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:06.000
Did you find it, then? Proof that he's alive?

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.130
Well...

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.460
I waited 2,000 years.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:11.920
But Sparda did not appear!

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:15.550
And so you're going after
Sparda's son, Dante?

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:22.730
That's right. If I get his soul, I'll
also get the dark knight Sparda's power.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.560
So you insist on this?

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.310
Yes.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.940
Then there's no help for it. In that case...

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:37.200
If you insist on this, then please
do it after you've defeated me.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.420
I have no desire to battle someone
who abandoned the way of the sword.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:58.550
When he gets back, tell him to come to me.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:49.060
I see... A duel with me, eh?

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.820
Please run.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:59.950
My brother should not fight you. And you...

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:03.950
What could you have to gain by fighting him?

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:07.460
Even if I don't have anything
to gain, he does, doesn't he?

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:11.380
Because word is that if he
gets my soul or whatever,

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:14.340
he'll get the same powers as my old man.

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.220
I don't know who spread that rumor,

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.760
but in the end, your brother's
another one who wants to capture it

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.140
and become king of the demon
world or something, am I right?

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.430
You don't understand
anything about my brother.

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:32.190
He just wants to fight someone strong.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:34.940
He has no thought of
ruling the demon world...

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:36.570
What about you?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.120
In truth, aren't you itching
even more than your brother is?

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.620
Itching for my soul.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.280
You're going to him, Dante?

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:24.870
When someone picks a fight
with me, I give it to them.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:25.660
That's the only reason I fight.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:42.890
I came, Milkman.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.060
Let's settle this thing
fast, before I catch a cold.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:52.730
What's wrong? Too scared to do anything
if your little brother isn't with you?

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.530
Heh, well this makes me happy.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.580
I've always wanted to know what a
swordsman trained by my father would be like.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:26.100
Looks like my father's
swordsmanship isn't that great.

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:30.140
I need you to give me
some more amusement here!

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:57.250
What's wrong? Done already?

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:01.210
I-I must not...

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:05.970
...lose here...

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:14.350
For the sake of Modeus as well,

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:18.190
Modeus who gave up the sword for me...

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:21.900
I must not...

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.740
be defeated here!

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.700
So you'll finally show your true nature, eh?

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:34.960
Brother...

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:43.510
I will surpass the dark knight Sparda!

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:27.680
Brother...

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:37.140
Two thousand years ago, when the
demon and human worlds were connected,

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:40.150
Sparda, my brother, and I made a promise.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:44.110
We promised we'd each live true to
our aspirations and carry them out.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:50.570
Soon afterwards, Sparda came to this
land all alone, to protect the human world.

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:55.160
And my brother never
aligned himself with either world,

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:58.660
merely waiting devotedly
for Sparda to return.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:04.840
Yes... Dueling with Sparda, the
best swordsman in the demon realm,

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.550
was his only reason for living.

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:09.340
I abandoned my sword.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.970
It had begun to disgust me.

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:16.560
It created nothing, and could even
rob my brother of his reason to live.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:24.480
And so since I killed your brother,
who was your reason to live...

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:30.650
...now your reason to live is
to take revenge against me?

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.280
You brothers couldn't be
any more old-fashioned.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.100
Morning, Dante!

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:10.570
Honestly! That Dante...

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:13.160
Wake up, Dante! Come on!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.080
Shut up. What the heck do you want?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:23.040
Today I'm making a special strawberry
sundae for that man in the black coat.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.460
Sheesh, no matter how much I clean
this place, you mess it right up again!

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.710
I don't think he'll come.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:32.760
Why not?

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.760
--A promise...
--Promise?

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:36.550
Yeah.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:44.100
He said he'd remembered an old
promise he made a long time ago.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:12.300
It's all going according to plan.

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:21.970
This is what I want.

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:25.230
Now there's only one more thing left.

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:06.290
You hear news about parents
abusing their children all the time,

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:11.500
but I still think I want to keep believing that
parents love their children unconditionally.

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:15.460
My mother died protecting me.

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:17.010
Maybe that's why...

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:21.220
I apparently have some humanity in me, too.

00:24:22.180 --> 00:24:25.060
And maybe Patty's mother abandoned Patty

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:28.060
because circumstances
made it unavoidable.

00:24:28.060 --> 00:24:30.060